    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.06) stands as our premier offensive anchor, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Valdez. His score is bolstered by a favorable park factor and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery profile that puts him in the green for stolen base attempts, a category where we remain hyper-aggressive to maintain our standing. **Daulton Varsho** (69.63) and **Dylan Beavers** (64.33) also project as high-ceiling plays; both capitalize on positive platoon splits against right-handed starters, and **Daulton Varsho** specifically benefits from an 87% success rate against his opponent's delivery tempo. While **Bryce Harper** (63.56) occupies the UTIL spot with a high-floor xwOBA of .390, the core strategy today relies on stacking these high-efficiency baserunners against matchups like Leahy and Houser to maximize our 5x5 leverage.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **JJ Bleday** (49.20), who nearly cracked the lineup. Despite his strong recent form, his negative platoon split against Castillo\u2019s handedness ultimately tipped the scales in favor of **Dylan Beavers**, who offers a more reliable platoon ceiling today. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.01) presented a compelling case due to his leadoff spot, but the optimizer prioritized the higher overall efficiency of our starting outfielders. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Lawrence Butler** (56.21); while his park factor is excellent, he faces a significantly lower-tier, tougher arm in Rasmussen, making him our most volatile start of the afternoon. We will continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan** as the lineups finalize, but we are well-positioned to capitalize on these specific matchup edges.",
